<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1363" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aeschĭnes</span></b> , is,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αὶσχίνης</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A disciple of Socrates</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Inv. 1,
				31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 5, 11, 27</span></i>.—But
			more celebrated, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The orator Æschines</i>, <i>rival to Demosthenes</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or.
				2, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 2,
				1, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 1,
				22</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A physician of Athens</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 28, 4,
				10, § 44</span></i>.</div>
